      <div type="clause" n="6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> 6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="454" ed="#liebermann"/>[6] Symle he sceal his hyrmen scyrpan mid manunge to hlafordes neode ⁊ him eac leanian be ðam ðe hy earnian.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="22.9" corresp="#wit-b">Symle he sceal his hyrmen scyr pan mid manunge to hlafordes neode .7 him eac leanian be ðam ðe hy earnian .</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="334" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Symle he sceal his hyrmen scyrpan mid manunge to hlafordes neode, and him eac leanian be ðam ðe hy earnian.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="454" ed="#liebermann"/>Immer soll er seine [Guts]unterthanen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Ger_6.lnote.de1.c"/> ermuntern durch Ermahnung zu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#Ger_6.lnote.de1.d"/> des Gutsherrn Bedarf und ihnen auch lohnen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#Ger_6.lnote.de1.e"/> je nachdem sie verdienen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">He must always urge on his [estate] dependants [peasants and demesne servants] by exhortation to the lord's needs, and also reward them according to what they earn.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">Similarly, he must inspire his underlings with admonishments to the lord’s need, and reward each of them as they merit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="335" ed="#rabin-doml"/>He must constantly encourage his subordinates with advice for his lord’s benefit, and reward each of them as they deserve.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Rect 6.3 and 20.2.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_6.lnote.de1.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">454</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bauern und Domänenknechte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">peasants and demesne servants</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_6.lnote.de1.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">454</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Rect. 6, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Rect. 6, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_6.lnote.de1.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">454</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi> 20, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> 20, 2</seg></note>
      </div>
